    "body": "## Problem\n\nAfter an edit, treesitter fold levels are recomputed only from near the edited lines. A fold that starts above that range and becomes foldable due to the edit (e.g. a Markdown section growing past 'foldminlines') is not created, and later lines get the wrong level.\n\n## Solution\n\nIf a fold starts above the recomputed range on a line that is not yet a fold start, recompute (and `foldupdate`) from that line.\n\nTest: `creates a fold that starts above the edited lines #42425` in `fold_spec.lua`.\n\nFixes #42425\n",
